KG42.register("rules-7303d552edb14fd576d28793",{"id":"08-real_time_prices::v141-c-R005","paper":"08-real_time_prices","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R005","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Consumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"Small end-consumers can participate by receiving and responding to five-minute real-time electricity price signals. Scope: Small end-consumer participation in the proposed EcoGrid EU bidless real-time market for balancing services. End-consumers can participate without creating bids or schedules. Scope: End-consumer participation in the proposed EcoGrid EU bidless market. All customers need five-minute meters to participate in this implementation. Scope: Customer participation in the proposed five-minute EcoGrid EU implementation; the requirement is stated for all customers. Condition: For the proposed five-minute implementation; adaptations using longer metering intervals remain possible. The expected balancing response imposes no physical or financial obligations on participating consumers' response behavior. Scope: Participating consumers included in the source's explicitly defined prosumer category; anticipated balancing-response behavior under constraint (2). Condition: For the response represented by the TSO's expected supply-demand balance constraint (2). Under the proposed restrictions, real-time market participation is limited to small prosumers, such as households; the source's prosumer category explicitly includes consumers. Scope: Consumer participation within the suggested anti-arbitrage rules separating the EcoGrid EU real-time market from the RP market. Condition: If the TSO adopts the proposed participation restrictions.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.consumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.price_signal","participation.consumer"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E001","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"participation.consumer","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev01","v141-b-g01-ev09"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Consumer participation within the suggested anti-arbitrage rules separating the EcoGrid EU real-time market from the RP market. | Customer participation in the proposed five-minute EcoGrid EU implementation; the requirement is stated for all customers. | End-consumer participation in the proposed EcoGrid EU bidless market. | Participating consumers included in the source's explicitly defined prosumer category; anticipated balancing-response behavior under constraint (2). | Small end-consumer participation in the proposed EcoGrid EU bidless real-time market for balancing services.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev01","v141-b-g01-ev09","v141-b-g01-ev12","v141-b-g01-ev16","v141-b-g01-ev30","v141-b-g02-ev-16","v141-b-g03-e07"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Small end-consumers can participate by receiving and responding to five-minute real-time electricity price signals. Scope: Small end-consumer participation in the proposed EcoGrid EU bidless real-time market for balancing services.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev01","v141-b-g01-ev09"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"End-consumers can participate without creating bids or schedules. Scope: End-consumer participation in the proposed EcoGrid EU bidless market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e07"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"All customers need five-minute meters to participate in this implementation. Scope: Customer participation in the proposed five-minute EcoGrid EU implementation; the requirement is stated for all customers. Condition: For the proposed five-minute implementation; adaptations using longer metering intervals remain possible.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev16"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The expected balancing response imposes no physical or financial obligations on participating consumers' response behavior. Scope: Participating consumers included in the source's explicitly defined prosumer category; anticipated balancing-response behavior under constraint (2). Condition: For the response represented by the TSO's expected supply-demand balance constraint (2).","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev12","v141-b-g02-ev-16"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Under the proposed restrictions, real-time market participation is limited to small prosumers, such as households; the source's prosumer category explicitly includes consumers. Scope: Consumer participation within the suggested anti-arbitrage rules separating the EcoGrid EU real-time market from the RP market. Condition: If the TSO adopts the proposed participation restrictions.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev12","v141-b-g01-ev30"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev01","location":{"location_id":"src-da8e4e26d6-p01-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"Abstract","anchor_text":"g g y g penetration of renewable generation. Additionally, the develop- ment in communication techno","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In this project, small-scale DERs and small end-consumers can actively participate in a new real-time electricity market by responding to 5-min real time electricity prices. In this way, the market operator will also obtain additional balancing power to cancel out the production variation introduced by renewable electricity generation."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev09","location":{"location_id":"src-da8e4e26d6-p02-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","anchor_text":"on and respond to real-time prices for providing balancing ser- ght vices. The bidless real time mar","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"It will include a new bidless real time market concept designed to incorporate end-consumers as well as small-scale DERs into the market structure by letting them receive and respond to real-time prices for providing balancing services. The bidless real time market will remove the barriers that end-consumers as well as small-scale DERs have previously been facing to enter the present market structure, e.g., requirements on size, and a significant administrative burden including bidding in the markets, complying with schedules, etc. The market tool will provide a transparent and simple mechanism to encourage the participation of small end-consumers and small-scale DERs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev12","location":{"location_id":"src-da8e4e26d6-p03-c1r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. REAL-TIME MARKET CONCEPT ARCHITECTURE","anchor_text":"2008 The participating prosumers (both consumers and producers) be will respond to the price signal ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The participating prosumers (both consumers and producers) will respond to the price signal for adjusting the real time consumption or production comparing with the day-ahead schedule and providing balancing power as a consequence. The time resolution of the real-time market is 5-min, which indicates the price will be updated frequently, every 5 minutes. In principle, the prosumers can take actions, such as turning off or on selected appliances, charging electric vehicles, etc., at any time according to the real-time electricity price. Since the electricity price can potentially change every 5 minutes, it is expected that automatic smart controllers will make the optimal decision based on the price signals and end-user's more static preferences, and subsequently control the DER units and/or smart appliances to change their electricity consumption or generation."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev16","location":{"location_id":"src-da8e4e26d6-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. REAL-TIME MARKET CONCEPT ARCHITECTURE","anchor_text":"consumption or production for each market interval, the real- m time price signal intervals must mat","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"All customers need 5-minute meters to participate in the new market. However, the fundamental concept and the infrastructure may work equally well with longer intervals, e.g., 10 minutes, though clearly the dynamic response for balancing will be limited by the interval length. This allows the concept to be replicated in areas where e.g., smart meters with 10-minute readings have already been deployed, and the concept can thereby be adapted to utilize such existing infrastructure."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev30","location":{"location_id":"src-da8e4e26d6-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M02-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. OPTIMIZATION MODELS FOR REAL-TIME PRICE SETTLEMENT AND FORECAST","anchor_text":"market and the existing RP market can provide arbitrage oppor- ta tunities. It is possible that the ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"To prevent price arbitrage between two markets, the TSO can set up market rules so that market players can only participate in only one market: RP market or real-time market. Specific market rules can be defined: The RP market addresses larger conventional generating units (above 10 MW). Only small prosumers e.g., households are subject to the general real-time price signal and participate in the real-time market. Moreover this problem would to a certain extent be mitigated by the current market rules: For participating in the RP market, the players (bulk physical suppliers) must submit their bids 45 mins before the operational hour. While real-time price signals are announced during the operational hour based on the system operational status, therefore it is not possible to use this information for create the bids in the RP market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev-16","location":{"location_id":"src-da8e4e26d6-p06-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-A. Real-Time Price Settlement Model","anchor_text":"1) (2) nd Note that the supply-demand balance constraint ((2)) is only nt the TSO’s expectation and ","equation_id":"Eq. (3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Note that the supply-demand balance constraint ((2)) is only the TSO's expectation and there is no physical or ﬁnancial obligations to prosumers at all associated with their behaviors. Removing these obligations by letting prosumers receive and respond to real-time prices will encourage the participation in the real time bidless market, which is one of the beneﬁts. However it will transfer the burden to TSO for predicting the aggregated prosumers' response. The accurate and effective of estimation of participants' behaviors is the prerequisite of a successful implementation of the proposed market concept."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-da8e4e26d6-p09-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"VI. Conclusion and Discussions","anchor_text":"real time price signal is sent to the prosumers in order to elimi- the nate the imbalance between th","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"The new bidless real-time electricity market is de- signed to allow the participation of small DERs as well as small end-consumer in a simple, efficient and low-cost way. It mini- mizes the efforts (transactions costs) put in by end-consumers and small-scale DERs, because they must not create bids and schedules, but simply respond to the real time price sent by TSO."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No design-selection or operational decision variables are declared for rule v141-c-R005. The rule is an admission/participation condition: the frozen nodes are coordination.price_signal and participation.consumer, and the source statements concern who may participate and under what metering and market-separation conditions. The source's decision variables (P^G, P^G,UR, P^G,DR, ΔP^L, ΔP^DER, λ^R, etc.) are declared in the clearing rule v141-c-R003 and are not re-scoped here.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed parameter objects are declared for rule v141-c-R005. The five-minute interval, the 10 MW RP-market threshold and the 45-minute bid deadline appear in the source as design/context numbers, but no typed parameter symbol or value is attached to this participation rule in the frozen graph. The day-ahead price λ^D and response coefficients α are declared in v141-c-R003, not this rule, so they are not reused across scopes."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-settlement","v141-a-M02-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.consumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev01","quote":"small-scale DERs and small end-consumers can actively participate in a new real-time electricity market by responding to 5-min real time electricity prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev09","quote":"It will include a new bidless real time market concept designed to incorporate end-consumers as well as small-scale DERs into the market structure by letting them receive and respond to real-time prices for providing balancing services."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e07","quote":"It mini- mizes the efforts (transactions costs) put in by end-consumers and small-scale DERs, because they must not create bids and schedules, but simply respond to the real time price sent by TSO."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev16","quote":"All customers need 5-minute meters to participate in the new market. However, the fundamental concept and the infrastructure may work equally well with longer intervals, e.g., 10 minutes, though clearly the dynamic response for balancing will be limited by the interval length."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev-16","quote":"Note that the supply-demand balance constraint ((2)) is only the TSO's expectation and there is no physical or ﬁnancial obligations to prosumers at all associated with their behaviors."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev12","quote":"The participating prosumers (both consumers and producers)"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev30","quote":"Specific market rules can be defined: The RP market addresses larger conventional generating units (above 10 MW). Only small prosumers e.g., households are subject to the general real-time price signal and participate in the real-time market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev12","quote":"The participating prosumers (both consumers and producers)"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"89e1a5e578d074c9b6f2a1ba6eca2542c950d537db0fb84ee5fd7537509442c1","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"Frozen rule v141-c-R005 is an admission/participation rule for small end-consumers in the EcoGrid EU real-time market. Its five phi constraints state eligibility, bidless participation, the 5-minute metering prerequisite, the absence of physical/financial obligations from balance constraint (2), and the proposed anti-arbitrage one-market restriction. The frozen graph contains only coordination.price_signal and participation.consumer as nodes and one 'links' edge; it declares no decision variables or fixed parameters, and the source supplies no algebraic eligibility, admission or obligation expression at this participation stage. The source's price-response equations for loads and DERs (e.g. Eq. (8)-(9)) are modeled in the separate clearing rule v141-c-R003 and cannot be moved into this rule without changing its scope. Missing mathematics is therefore not inferred. B evidence remains unreviewed in this experiment.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal","participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R005-E001"],"rationale":"C001 is the core 'links' relation in the frozen graph: coordination.price_signal links to participation.consumer through edge v141-c-R005-E001; both member nodes are present."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 states the bidless character of consumer participation; it is a condition on the participation.consumer node. The frozen graph defines no bid/schedule node or edge in this rule, so only that node is bound."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C003","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C003 attaches the five-minute metering prerequisite to consumer participation; it is a condition on the participation.consumer node. No metering node or edge exists in this frozen rule graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C004","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C004 states the absence of physical/financial obligations on participating consumers; it is a condition on the participation.consumer node. The referenced balance constraint (2) belongs to the clearing model and is not an edge of this rule graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C005","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C005 states the anti-arbitrage participation limitation for consumers; it is a condition on the participation.consumer node. The RP-market counterpart is outside this rule's frozen node set, so no cross-market edge is bound."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
